rauders map which is an important  plot device and holds importance  throughout the series  where they are what they're doing every  minute of every day brilliant  an introduction to hogsmeade as well as  other important locations that will make  a later return  such as the shrieking shack and the  three broomsticks  we also see a number of fantastical  beasts added primarily buckbeak  and the monster book which serves as the  prelude to the fantastic beasts series  we also see the expansion of hogwarts  classes with divination brilliantly  introduced through emma thompson's zany  performance as professor trelawney the  future  we are introduced to further magical  abilities and curses with sirius black  and peter pettigrew being an animagus  while remus  lupin is cursed as a werewolf also their  true identities are cleverly coded in  their  names with remus being a reference to  the founders of rome  romulus and remus who were raised by  wolves and lupin is the french word for  wolf like sirius is also a reference to  the star constellation which is also  known as the big dog  and black is well the color looks so  like your father overall the movie has  a lot going for it it is one of the best  and most popular books  a great story a deep world a brilliant  director  sensational visuals and outstanding  performances and  all of these elements together add up to  arguably the best harry potter movie  at the end of the day though it is still  subjective and the quality between the  movies is nominally close  and undoubtedly people will rightly  dispute the claim that this is the best  harry potter movie do you agree that  azkaban is the best in the series  do you think azkaban did a good job of  imagining the wizarding world  or did another movie do it best do you  wish quran had done another  harry potter movie let us know in the  comments below and make sure to  subscribe to the channel for  everything magical  you

